  "id": "COMPOUND:25148 - PROTEIN:685",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a complex network of interactions where the compound in question is a target of multiple substances, all of which ultimately lead to the Serine/threonine-protein phosphatase 2A catalytic subunit beta isoform. This compound is identified as a target of three different agents: N-[(3-hydroxy-4-methoxyphenyl)methyl]-7-methyloctanamide, Spongia-13(16),14-Dien-19-Oic Acid, and Quinaldic Acid. These agents are themselves targets of the same final entity, which implies a potential pathway of action through the phosphatase enzyme. The evidence is consistent across multiple paths, indicating that the compound may be involved in a regulatory process that modulates the activity of the phosphatase. The strength of the evidence is supported by the high scores in all three paths, suggesting a robust relationship. However, the exact mechanism by which the compound interacts with the phosphatase remains unclear, and further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the precise role of this interaction.",
